        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9923167c-fc5e-505d-9894-26a5eb3970cb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: National Gas Turbine Establishment, Royal Aircraft Establishment, Power Jets, Royal Air Force\n- People: Frank Whittle, Hayne Constant\n- Places: Fleet, UK\n- Topics: gas turbine and jet engine design and development\n\nFacts:\n- Air Commodore Sir Frank Whittle was born on 1 June 1907 and died on 9 August 1996.\n- Frank Whittle was an English Royal Air Force engineer air officer.\n- The National Gas Turbine Establishment, also called NGTE Pyestock, was in Fleet and was part of the Royal Aircraft Establishment.\n- The National Gas Turbine Establishment was created by merging the design teams of Frank Whittle's Power Jets and the Royal Aircraft Establishment turbine development team run by Hayne Constant.\n- The National Gas Turbine Establishment was the prime site in the UK for the design and development of gas turbine and jet engines.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
